      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-06T15:26:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like the ordering changed here. Could this create a problem with the netd implementation that runs on R?\n\nAlso - looks like the new code first gets the stats and then removes the rule. But while we\u0027re fetching the stats, the rule could still be forwarding traffic. So the stats could be incorrect. Is there something we can do about this?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "295facd7_7db49e86",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1961665
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-08T13:42:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about we change the order of handling in BpfCoordinator#updateAllIpv6Rules? We handle downstream rules change before upstream rules change. But there is still one different compare to the previous code. In previous code, when there is upstream interface but no downstream neighbor, it won\u0027t write the upstream rule to bpf map and won\u0027t set quota limit on the upstream interface, but now we\u0027ll have those bpf maps.\n\nAbout the second concern on the stats correctness, it won\u0027t have issue, because bpf won\u0027t forward traffic if there is no stats entry on the upstream:\n```\nTetherStatsValue* stat_v \u003d bpf_tether_stats_map_lookup_elem(\u0026stat_and_limit_k);\n// If we don\u0027t have anywhere to put stats, then abort...\nif (!stat_v) TC_PUNT(NO_STATS_ENTRY);\n```",
      "parentUuid": "71f2866d_66266499",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "646e3190_8448669d",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T11:05:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If BPF won\u0027t forward traffic if there is no stats entry, then I think doing things in either order is probably OK, as long as the old netd implementation in R works OK.\n\nDo you think one order is more correct than the other? Or are you just suggesting we match the previous behaviour so the netd implementation in R doesn\u0027t see a behaviour change?",
      "parentUuid": "295facd7_7db49e86",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "295dd330_45b5a075",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1961665
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T14:38:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think both orders are okay, my suggestion is just to match previous behavior if we have concern for implementation of old netd in R. So maybe we keep the change in current CL?",
      "parentUuid": "646e3190_8448669d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3837fd5d_0837bb06",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T09:45:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I just happened to see this comment in the v31 BpfCoordinatorShimImpl:\n\n\n        // getAndClearTetherOffloadStats is called after all offload rules have already been\n        // deleted for the given upstream interface. Before starting to do cleanup stuff in this\n        // function, use synchronizeKernelRCU to make sure that all the current running eBPF\n        // programs are finished on all CPUs, especially the unfinished packet processing. After\n        // synchronizeKernelRCU returned, we can safely read or delete on the stats map or the\n        // limit map.\n        final int res \u003d synchronizeKernelRCU();\n        if (res !\u003d 0) {\n            // Error log but don\u0027t return. Do as much cleanup as possible.\n            mLog.e(\"synchronize_rcu() failed: \" + res);\n        }\n\nThere\u0027s a similar comment in the old R netd implementation:\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/base/+/rvc-dev:system/netd/server/TetherController.cpp;l\u003d1173\n\n\nBasically, the current code tries to ensure that the BPF code will not forward any packets before the stats are read and cleared. I think we need to continue to do this. Can we do this by changing the order in updateAllIpv6Rules (and in clearIpv6Rules) so that it does downstream rules first, then upstream? If so, let\u0027s do that... and add a comment to ensure we don\u0027t forget this again.",
      "parentUuid": "295dd330_45b5a075",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b35d286_eba21ded",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T10:33:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion, I think updateAllIpv6Rules should:\n\n- delete the downstream rules (and save them)\n- delete the upstream rules (which fetches the stats)\n- put the rules back\n\nI *think* that when it puts the rules back, it should probably first put the upstream rules back, which adds the limit, before adding the downstream rules, right? Or does it not matter?",
      "parentUuid": "3837fd5d_0837bb06",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64b238b6_e5955183",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 806,
      "author": {
        "id": 1961665
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T13:33:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. I think when it puts the rules back, it is better that the upstream rules are put back first, eliminates the possibilities that there are downstream rules but no stats entry, although it probably won\u0027t cause any issue (the network stack will handle the packet when it happens).",
      "parentUuid": "7b35d286_eba21ded",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 806,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 806,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae1bf30a_f2c2a9f0",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 1107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-06T15:26:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it correct to send the quota even if there are no downstream rules? I\u0027d guess the new implementation will be fine. Will the old netd implementation behave correctly as well?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1107,
        "startChar": 65,
        "endLine": 1107,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bae284e_ff6299a8",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 1107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1961665
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-11T03:24:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After checking the corresponding netd functions in R, it seems that the only write sequence we should follow is setBpfLimit must be call before getAndClearTetherOffloadStats for an upstream, otherwise it will return error. For ingress, stats and limit maps usage in do_forward function in offload.c, if there is no map entry for either one of them, it simply lets the core stack handle the packet. So I think it is okay if there are stats\u0026limit maps but no ingress(downstream) map.\n\n[addOffloadRule](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/base/+/rvc-dev:system/netd/server/TetherController.cpp;bpv\u003d0;l\u003d854)\n[removeOffloadRule](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/base/+/rvc-dev:system/netd/server/TetherController.cpp;bpv\u003d0;l\u003d879)\n[setBpfLimit](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/base/+/rvc-dev:system/netd/server/TetherController.cpp;bpv\u003d0;l\u003d1054)\n[getAndClearTetherOffloadStats](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/base/+/rvc-dev:system/netd/server/TetherController.cpp;bpv\u003d0;l\u003d1165)\n\n[do_forward](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/base/+/rvc-dev:system/netd/bpf_progs/offload.c;bpv\u003d0;l\u003d37)\n```\n    TetherIngressValue* v \u003d bpf_tether_ingress_map_lookup_elem(\u0026k);\n    // If we don\u0027t find any offload information then simply let the core stack handle it...\n    if (!v) return TC_ACT_OK;\n\n    uint32_t stat_and_limit_k \u003d skb-\u003eifindex;\n    TetherStatsValue* stat_v \u003d bpf_tether_stats_map_lookup_elem(\u0026stat_and_limit_k);\n    // If we don\u0027t have anywhere to put stats, then abort...\n    if (!stat_v) return TC_ACT_OK;\n\n    uint64_t* limit_v \u003d bpf_tether_limit_map_lookup_elem(\u0026stat_and_limit_k);\n    // If we don\u0027t have a limit, then abort...\n    if (!limit_v) return TC_ACT_OK;\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ae1bf30a_f2c2a9f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1107,
        "startChar": 65,
        "endLine": 1107,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "8aca86b35849c72e7ba70f7cf6eede846fb0775d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5e8f5269_b5a73dcd",
        "filename": "Tethering/tests/unit/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfCoordinatorTest.java",
